    "workspaces": [
      { "id": "studio-guide", "name": "Start here — Interactive Studio", "type": "text-editor", "x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 450, "height": 550, "contents": [], "editor": { "name": "README.txt", "sourceWorkspaceId": null, "sourceFileId": null, "text": "INTERACTIVE STUDIO\n\n1. Open Shared Knobs fullscreen and move amplitude, frequency, damping.\n2. Open Spring Simulation and Play. These controls also drive Live Curve.\n3. Capture data in Simulation, then import it from Simulation Samples.\n4. Open Parameter Animation and Play. Its tracks feed the control panel, so both plot and simulation animate together. Pause before editing knobs yourself.\n5. HTML Spring is a sandboxed mini-app responding to the same controls.\n6. Audio Synth has its own pitch/gain controls; click Start audio explicitly.\n7. Dashboard assembles the plot and captured data.\n\nSave JSON stores settings and captured outputs. Animation/audio never auto-start when loading.\n\nTo record manual knob movements, create a second Timeline, connect Shared Knobs → it, and press Record incoming controls. Avoid creating a feedback loop with the animation timeline." } },
      { "id": "studio-timeline", "name": "Parameter Animation", "type": "timeline", "x": 0, "y": 700, "width": 450, "height": 450, "contents": [], "tool": { "kind": "timeline", "settings": { "duration": 10, "loop": true }, "text": "[{\"name\":\"amplitude\",\"from\":0.5,\"to\":3},{\"name\":\"frequency\",\"from\":0.5,\"to\":2.5}]", "output": "{}" } },
